From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 18:03:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] camera: Take frames from the host's camera service

Deckard's camera provider, android.hardware.camera.provider-V1-deckard-service
(ICameraProvider/deckard/0), is AOSP's AIDL external camera HAL with V4L2
swapped for deckard-camera on the host: libcamera owns the sensors, and
each frame arrives over /data/deckard/camera.sock as a dma-buf (RGBA),
which the HAL maps and converts once to its full-range I420 working frame.
Cropping, scaling, the YUV and JPEG outputs and EXIF stay AOSP's.

Cameras follow the host's list, back first, as device@1.1/internal/<n>;
facing and sensor orientation are libcamera's Location and Rotation. A
camera the host has lent elsewhere opens as CAMERA_IN_USE. The cameras
are present while a connection to the host is open.

Also fixes switchToOffline wrapping a frame it does not own in a second
shared_ptr.
